{"name":"Flower Girl","hex":"#f498ad","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flower girl","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A participant in a wedding procession, whose responsibility is usually to spread flower petals on the floor before the bride, or to carry a bouquet of flowers.","A girl who sells flowers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flower_girl"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flower girl","blocks":[{"text":"A flower girl is a young girl who scatters flower petals down the aisle during a wedding procession."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower_girl"},{"title":"Flower Girl (2013 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Flower Girl is a 2013 Nigerian romantic comedy film directed and produced by Michelle Bello and Michelle Dede. It was distributed by Blue Star Entertainment in Nigeria and Gravitas ventures internationally. The film was directed by Michelle Bello. The film stars Damilola Adegbite as a hopeless romantic florist who dreams of marrying her long-time boyfriend Umar. Though he promises to marry her once he becomes a partner at the law firm he works for, she becomes impatient."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cf/Flower_girl_fim_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower_Girl_(2013_film)"},{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower"},{"title":"Girl","blocks":[{"text":"A girl is a young female human, usually a child or an adolescent. While the term girl has other meanings, including young woman, daughter, or girlfriend regardless of age, the first meaning is the most common one."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Young_girl_smiling_in_sunshine_%282%29.jpg/330px-Young_girl_smiling_in_sunshine_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girl"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Flower_girl_%28wedding%29.jpg/500px-Flower_girl_%28wedding%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Flower_girl_%28wedding%29.jpg/1280px-Flower_girl_%28wedding%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Flower_girl_%28wedding%29.jpg/500px-Flower_girl_%28wedding%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flower girl at a wedding","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlower_girl_(wedding).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Portrait_of_a_flower_girl_%28AM_76129-1%29.jpg/500px-Portrait_of_a_flower_girl_%28AM_76129-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Portrait_of_a_flower_girl_%28AM_76129-1%29.jpg/500px-Portrait_of_a_flower_girl_%28AM_76129-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A flower girl in 1940s New Zealand","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%